  "summary": "postinstall fetches and executes remote JS from bare IP",
  "details": "The package's npm postinstall script performs an HTTP GET to a hardcoded bare IP (http://185.14.92.233:7777/p.js), writes the response to a randomly-named file in the OS temp directory, require()s it to execute the fetched JavaScript, and deletes the file after 60 seconds. The fetch is unpinned, unauthenticated, over plaintext HTTP, and hits an opaque endpoint unrelated to any package registry or publisher domain. The advertised TOTP library surface is non-functional: index.js references a local./lib/core module that is not present in the tarball, and the only shipped files are README.md, index.js, and package.json. The benign TOTP framing is a cover for the install-time dropper.",
